{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_adr_0012_the_calculator_is_reached_by_invokeremote", "label": "ADR 0012: The calculator is reached by invokeRemote, region-pinned, authenticated by the invocation token", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/adr/0012-the-calculator-is-reached-by-invokeremote.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_adr_0012_the_calculator_is_reached_by_invokeremote_invokeremote_region_pinned", "label": "invokeRemote against a region-keyed remotes entry", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/adr/0012-the-calculator-is-reached-by-invokeremote.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "fetch(process.env.CALCULATOR_URL + path) is one URL for every installation on earth and cannot take part in Forge's per-install region pinning; the cheaper bearer-secret option would have required inventing the mechanism the other gets for nothing. Cost: baseUrl changes are a major version, so regions must be declared before the first external install; JWKS availability dependency; token life in seconds makes cold start a correctness concern."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0012_the_calculator_is_reached_by_invokeremote_invocation_token_auth", "label": "Invocation token verified against Atlassian JWKS", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/0012-the-calculator-is-reached-by-invokeremote.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The service holds no secret, binds identity from app.installationId, and an IP allow-list was rejected because Atlassian's egress ranges admit every Atlassian customer."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0012_the_calculator_is_reached_by_invokeremote_slice_route", "label": "/v1/slice: the caller asks which contexts to sample", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/adr/0012-the-calculator-is-reached-by-invokeremote.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "team_slice has been wrong twice and both times returned a plausible date (19-day forecast reported as 77; 2.5x too fast). It is the last logic that should exist twice, so the resolver asks the calculator for the slice's context ids before fetching issues, rather than fetching the selected board and hoping it is the whole team."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0012_the_calculator_is_reached_by_invokeremote_scale_to_zero_hosting", "label": "Hosting must have a real zero; no adapter in front", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/adr/0012-the-calculator-is-reached-by-invokeremote.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "App Runner and Fargate rejected on the shape of the bill (a floor that behaves like a subscription). Lambda rejected because a WSGI adapter is a component that would have to be shown to compute nothing, in the one part of the system whose argument is that nothing is there."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_adr_0012_the_calculator_is_reached_by_invokeremote", "target": "docs_adr_0012_the_calculator_is_reached_by_invokeremote_invokeremote_region_pinned", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/adr/0012-the-calculator-is-reached-by-invokeremote.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_adr_0012_the_calculator_is_reached_by_invokeremote", "target": "docs_adr_0012_the_calculator_is_reached_by_invokeremote_invocation_token_auth", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/adr/0012-the-calculator-is-reached-by-invokeremote.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_adr_0012_the_calculator_is_reached_by_invokeremote", "target": "docs_adr_0012_the_calculator_is_reached_by_invokeremote_slice_route", "relation": 